#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521743 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00042721-b3b3-5fbd-b6e7-5fc25785342e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨15,102⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 3,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521675} {:answer/id #uuid "32a582f3-ec49-5904-99aa-53c73288aae3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨-15,102⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 3,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521690} {:answer/id #uuid "4b48aec1-60e5-583c-ada6-a775d24ebc37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨15,102⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 3,\\,y + 3⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521692} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd2df2a-bf80-53d8-92cf-7e86fd6efaab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨15,102⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 3,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521705} {:answer/id #uuid "90b092f8-0fdd-5bdc-a2ce-b5869f85c49f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "⟨102,15⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 3,\\,y - 3⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521720}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521675} :answer-field/id #uuid "e75251e7-9449-527e-a205-be7072ce45be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521741}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ed4b53f0-5376-5776-9478-e43f57923282" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y)=- 5 x^{2} + 5 x y^{2} + 2 y^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(3,3).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(3,3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 5 x^{2} + 5 x y^{2} + 2 y^{2})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 5 x^{2} + 5 x y^{2} + 2 y^{2})\\,j \\\\  & =(- 10 x + 5 y^{2})\\,i+(10 x y + 4 y)\\,j \\\\ ∇f(3,3) & =(- 10 (3) + 5 (3)^{2})\\,i+(10 (3) (3) + 4 (3))\\,j \\\\  & =(15)\\,i+(102)\\,j \\\\  & =⟨15,102⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(3,3)\\cdot ⟨x-(3),\\,y-(3)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨15,102⟩\\cdot ⟨x - 3,\\,y - 3⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a4137d-ddb6-53e9-8eba-31dd118da976" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(2,-2)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521751} {:answer/id #uuid "0963e65c-d280-54c5-8d17-93cf19eca363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(1,0)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521752} {:answer/id #uuid "49c63c1d-850a-5467-bc9f-8d6c96a23564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(1,-1)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521792} {:answer/id #uuid "4d7bc285-d4bb-52bd-b477-8eb6442fca3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(-1,1)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521795} {:answer/id #uuid "613efcec-87ab-524f-80ad-5c6c7ea407fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$(1,1)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521806}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521792} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b54fca1-5f4f-5f7a-ac16-b56cb534ed89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0e539d3d-4951-53af-94a7-c8aeb37adea8" :question/problem "At which point on the curve $8 x y + 4 y^{2}=- 4 x^{2} + 2 y + 2$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}8 x y + 4 y^{2}&=- 4 x^{2} + 2 y + 2\\\\4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 2 y - 2&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 2 y - 2$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 2 y - 2)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 x^{2} + 8 x y + 4 y^{2} - 2 y - 2)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 8 y - 2)\\,i-(8 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\- 8 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=-x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}4(x+(-x))^{2}-2(-x)-(2)&=0\\\\2x-(2)&=0\\\\2x&=2\\\\x&=1\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding point is $(1,-1)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521758 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5244335d-6970-5429-aa03-d3dec60b6ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521799} {:answer/id #uuid "dbde3a30-d25a-522f-935f-3e8b50dc20ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521858}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521799} :answer-field/id #uuid "0442c6bd-1b78-5c99-ad02-d114eb9446c8" :answer-field/key "$(3,0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521747} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bcca2dc-e93a-558e-afac-54ae144ba53f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521775} {:answer/id #uuid "ab244f97-43eb-57ac-828c-fe7913efb4d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521837}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521775} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b9b35e0-eec0-5034-8f33-49c3f